sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch03-01> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch03-01--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch03-01--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch03-01: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.62" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.624"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.66"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Open matrix-population and abundance databases can test geometrical potential versus realized numbers for hundreds of species, and the calculation is standard. The universal scope is only sampled, and the tripartite 'struggle' is hard to refute because every limit falls into one of the three bins. The resolvable part is overproduction, not the exhaustive classification of checks." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Compare potential population growth at low density, from fecundity and survival schedules, with realized long-term abundance. Potential growth well above replacement, with realized numbers checked by conspecifics, other species, or physical factors, would support the argument; life histories whose maximum growth is at or below replacement would refute universal geometrical overproduction." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "The struggle is said to be with conspecifics, other species, or physical conditions, a disjunction that covers every possible check.", "Demographic matrices are biased toward plants, vertebrates, and temperate studies.", "Potential growth estimated from a short study can misrepresent the long-run tendency to increase." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch03-01--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch03-01--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch03-01--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch03-01--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch03-01 by Grok 4.7: 0.66" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.66"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch03-01--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch03-01> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch03-01--grok--operationalizability> .
